/volume><issue>18</issue><fpage>3091</fpage><lpage>3094</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3463305</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nakagawa</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Wachi</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Woo</surname><given-names>J-T</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Fenton reaction is primarily involved in a mechanism of (3)-epigallocatechin-3-gallate to induce osteoclastic cell death</article-title><source><italic>Biochemical &#x00026; Biophysical Research Communications</italic></source><year>2002</year><volume>292</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>94</fpage><lpage>101</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11890677</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yun</surname><given-names>J-H</given-names></name><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>C-S</given-names></name><name><surname>Cho</surname><given-names>K-S</given-names></name><name><surname>Chai</surname><given-names>J-K</given-names></name><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>C-K</given-names></name><name><surname>Choi</surname><given-names>S-H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>(-)-Epigallocatechin gallate induces apoptosis, via caspase activation, in osteoclasts differentiated from RAW 264.7 cells</article-title><source><italic>Journal of Periodontal Research</italic></source><year>2007</year><volume>42</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>212</fpage><lpage>218</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17451540</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Morinobu</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Biao</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Tanaka</surname><given-name